To run the author tests you will need a JSON file describing your Payr
sandbox credentials, structured as follows:

    /path/to/working/business-payr > cat business-payr-credentials.json
    {
        "api_token"   : "your_sandbox_server_api_token",
        "api_host"    : "sandbox-api.mypayr.co.uk",
        "iframe_host" : "sandbox.mypayr.co.uk"
    }

Contact support@mypayr.co.uk to request sandbox access and obtain your
initial server API token.

Once you have the credentials file, set the PAYR_CREDENTIALS environment
variable to its path and run the author tests with prove:

    PAYR_CREDENTIALS=business-payr-credentials.json prove -lr xt/

The author tests are designed to be run in order:

    xt/000_changes.t         - Verifies the Changes file is correctly formatted
    xt/001_onboard.t         - Onboards test users into the sandbox environment
    xt/002_payment_session.t - Creates payment sessions for onboarded users
                               (requires xt/001_onboard.t to have been run first)
    xt/003_rotate_token.t    - Rotates the server API token

NOTE: xt/003_rotate_token.t will rotate the API token stored in your
credentials file.  After running it, update the "api_token" value in your
credentials file with the new token printed in the test output.  The old
token remains valid for a grace period of 7-15 days.

To run a single author test file:

    PAYR_CREDENTIALS=business-payr-credentials.json prove -lv xt/001_onboard.t
